{
 "product_id": "p-adhd-001",
 "items": [
  {
   "key": "must:mh_dated",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Dated 2027, Monday-start, every date linked: year page to month, month to its weeks, week to each day, day to the next and previous day."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_multi_year",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Covers two years: Nov and Dec 2026 head-start month and week pages before the full 2027 year (14 months in all), so a buyer in late October can start this week instead of waiting for January."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_apps",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "One landscape PDF that works in Goodnotes (named first in title and listing), Notability, Samsung Notes, Xodo and Noteshelf on iPad, Android and Windows tablets."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_adhd",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "ADHD-specific on the page, not only in the title: every day has Today's top 3, time blocks, a brain dump box, an energy rating and one win."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_core",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "The core set buyers praise and use daily: year at a glance, 12 month pages with side tabs, every week, every day, a habit tracker per month, an energy map for the year, brain dump and notes pages."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_look",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "A finished, designed look with real typography and consistent spacing; design is the single biggest praise driver."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_guide",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Instructions printed inside the file, not only in a video or a separate PDF."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_hard",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_hard: Every day page has the same seven boxes in the same places (Today's top 3, Time blocks 7am to 9pm, Brain dump, Energy 1 to 5 with Basics, One win today, Dopamine break), so there is one page to learn. The cover's Open planner button lands on the 4-step Start here page, and every page carries Home, the month tabs and a Month / Week breadcrumb."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_download",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_download: Listing copy and photo 4 give the download in 3 steps: buy, download from Etsy in a web browser (the Etsy app cannot download digital files), open the PDF in a planner app. It ships as one PDF, not a zip, under 19.5 MB so it downloads and imports quickly. The Start here page repeats the steps for anyone who opened it on a computer first."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_misleading",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_misleading: Every listing photo is a screenshot of the built file, captioned with the page name; no mockup shows anything the file lacks. The description lists each page type with counts and says plainly: landscape only, Monday-start weeks, Nov to Dec 2026 has month and week pages (no day pages), no stickers, handwrite or use the app's text tool (not a fillable form). Photo 10 repeats this next to the Contents page."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_device",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_device: Pages are 1024 x 768 landscape (4:3, the iPad's own shape) so there are no big empty margins, and all tabs and dates are plain PDF links. The listing has a Works with / Not for box: works in Goodnotes, Notability, Samsung Notes, Xodo and Noteshelf on iPad, Android and Windows tablets; not made for phones, e-ink tablets, or viewing in Files, Photos or Google Drive preview. The Setup check page proves it on the buyer's own device in one minute."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_not_useful",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_not_useful: Month tabs run down the right edge of every page (answering 'there are no monthly tabs so you are swiping through the pages'), and year, month, week and day pages are all linked to each other. It is dated, so there is nothing to set up: open today and write. The Contents page shows every section and month on one screen."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_setup",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_setup: Start here (4 numbered steps: open it in a planner app, check the links, pen off to tap and on to write, plan one day) and Setup check are the first two cards on the Contents page and the pages right after it. 'Where are the stickers?' cannot happen: there are none, and the listing says so."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_quality",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_quality: Pages run in strict date order: Nov to Dec 2026 head start, then each 2027 month followed by its weeks and their days, and each week and day page appears exactly once (the line currently prints the 8 weeks that span two months twice; see build_notes). The build checks 0 broken links and no overflowing text, and all text is vector so it stays crisp at any zoom."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_support",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_support: Most support messages are 'it does not work' questions, so the answers are in the file and the listing: the Setup check page's 'Nothing happened?' list (pen off, open in a planner app, import as PDF, then message us), the Start here steps, and a listing FAQ with the top five problems (Etsy app download, which app, links not tapping, how to type, landscape only). How fast the shop replies is shop-level (Darren's Etsy inbox), not something the file can fix."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_value",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_value: Priced at $14, well under the $22 median, for a full dated 2027 with day pages plus a 2026 head start. Writing space, the thing a $14 buyer said was missing, is generous: half of each day page is open writing (brain dump, time blocks), each weekday gets its own lined box on the week page, and text is set at 1.1 scale. Photo 2 shows a day page at real size so buyers can judge the space before buying."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_nav",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_nav: Three ways to move on every month, week and day page: month tabs down the right edge, a top bar (Home, Year, Restart, Dopamine, Energy, Brain dump, Notes), and a breadcrumb (January / Week 3) that works as a back button. Day pages add previous and next arrows, every date on the year page jumps to its day, and the Contents page links every section and month."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_overwhelm",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_overwhelm: Short on purpose: nine page types (year, month, habit tracker, week, day, dopamine menu, routines, energy map, brain dump and notes) instead of dozens of templates, seven boxes per day page, and a Contents page that fits on one screen. Start here says 'plan one day' and the Restart page says 'do not catch up'. The listing says: not 50 templates, just the pages you will use every day."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_edit",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_edit: The Start here page says how to write and type: pen on to write, pen off to tap links, the app's text tool to type. Anything personal is left blank to fill in (habit names, the month's one goal, about half of each dopamine menu and routine column), so buyers customize by writing, not by editing the PDF. The listing says it is not a fillable form."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_broken",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_broken: The Setup check page has three buttons (a month, the year, Contents) that jump and come back, plus the 'Nothing happened?' fix list. Every link in the file is checked at build (0 broken links allowed)."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_start",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "Five-minute start and setup check: Page 3 is a 4-step Start here guide and page 4 is a Setup check page with buttons that jump and return, plus a fix list if they do not. The cover's Open planner button lands on Start here."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_day",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "One calm ADHD day page: The same seven boxes every day: Today's top 3, Time blocks 7am to 9pm, Brain dump, Energy 1 to 5 with Basics (meds, water, a real meal), One win today and Dopamine break. The week page mirrors it with This week's top 3, a Weekly reset and Not this week."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_restart",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "Fell off? Start again page: A one-page, no-guilt way back in, in the top bar as Restart: skip the gap and do not catch up, jump to today in two taps, write one thing in Today's top 3, empty your head into the brain dump. Its tip points to the weekly reset for longer breaks."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_dopamine",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "Dopamine menu and routines: A Dopamine menu page (Quick 5 min, Medium 20 min, Big rewards, Costs you later) and a Routines page (Morning, Leaving the house, Evening wind-down), each column part pre-filled and part blank to make your own. The day page's Dopamine break box is where you note the one you picked."
  },
  {
   "key": "look",
   "kind": "look",
   "text": "Calm and clear, not cute and not beige. Warm cream paper (not white, so it glows less in a dark room) with deep slate ink at 13:1 contrast so it stays sharp in daylight; muted text is still 5.3:1. Structure is soft teal (filled boxes like Today's top 3 are pale teal), with one small coral accent bar on the Contents and guide pages. Month tabs run from teal to periwinkle, a cool, quiet range rather than a rainbow, with dark ink labels on every tab. Fraunces headings add warmth; Outfit body text is wide and easy to read at 1.1 scale. Square, plain decoration (motif 'lines'): no florals, no clip-art."
  }
 ],
